## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to model non-crossing, higher-arity structures with DP and reconstruct a solution.

## Key Concepts

- DP state dp[i][t] for i and t
- Non-crossing triple formation
- Reconstruction via backpointers
- Time/space trade-offs and optimization path

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxTriples(A, n, k) {
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prv = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++) {
    for (let t=0; t<=k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
      if (t>0) {
        for (let i1=1; i1<i; i1++) {
          for (let j=i1+1; j<i; j++) {
            const prev = (i1>=2 ? dp[i1-1][t-1] : (t-1===0 ? 0 : -Infinity));
            const val = prev + A[i1-1]*A[j-1]*A[i-1];
            if (val > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = val; prv[i][t] = {i1, j}; }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction logic would backtrack using prv
  return {value: dp[n][k], triples: []};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests advanced tree DP with a connectivity constraint and a knapsack-like merge across children. Requires careful reconstruction of the chosen nodes.

## Key Concepts

- Tree DP: dp[u][s] for connected subgraphs containing u within its subtree
- Knapsack-like merging of children to combine subtree sizes
- Path reconstruction: storing decisions to recover node set
- Complexity: O(nk) time and O(nk) space; handle negative values with offset

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxConnectedSubtreeSum(n, k, edges, val) {
  const g = Array.from({ length: n }, () => []);
  for (const [u, v] of edges) { g[u].push(v); g[v].push(u); }
  const parent = Array(n).fill(-1);
  const order = [];
  function dfs(u, p) {
    parent[u] = p;
    for (const v of g[u]) if (v !== p) dfs(v, u);
    order.push(u);
  }
  dfs(0, -1);
  // dp[u] will be an array of length min(subtreeSize[u], k) + 1
  // Initialization, merging and reconstruction would follow a standard tree knapsack pattern
  // Full implementation is lengthy; outline focuses on the recurrence above
  return { best: null, nodes: [] };
}
```

