## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical DP with fixed-length window constraints and reconstruction, mirroring analytics batching scenarios.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes with exact segment count
- Prefix sums for fast interval sums
- Reconstruction path tracking

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarraysWithBounds(A, k, L, R){
  const n = A.length;
  const P = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) P[i] = P[i-1] + A[i-1];
  const neg = -1/0; const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(neg));
  for(let i=0;i<=n;i++) dp[i][0] = 0;
  const take = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=k;t++){
      dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
      for(let len=L; len<=R && len<=i; len++){
        if (dp[i-len][t-1] !== neg) {
          const val = dp[i-len][t-1] + (P[i]-P[i-len]);
          if (val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; take[i][t] = len; }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return {maxSum: dp[n][k], take}
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests translating a DP state into a practical recurrence with non-overlap constraint and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts

- DP over index i and count t
- Non-overlapping constraint handled by dp[i-2] for taking a domino
- Backtracking to recover indices

## Code Example

```javascript
function solve(A, k){
  const n=A.length;
  const NEG=-1e15;
  const dp=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const take=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(false));
  for(let i=0;i<=n;i++) dp[i][0]=0;
  for(let i=2;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=k;t++){
      const v1=dp[i-1][t];
      const v2=dp[i-2][t-1]+A[i-2]+A[i-1];
      if(v2>v1){ dp[i][t]=v2; take[i][t]=true; }
      else dp[i][t]=v1;
    }
  }
  // backtrack
  // ... reconstruct domino starts from i=n, t=k
  return dp[n][k];
}
```

